course: dictionary
lesson: 6795
title: A hard experience, and an old test
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ordeal is a very hard, painful or frightening experience that goes on for some time. Read the clues around it. In «a terrible ordeal», the word terrible tells you the experience was bad, so ordeal means something you must get through and survive.
explain: Sometimes people use the word jokingly. «The car journey was an ordeal» does not mean the trip was dangerous. It means the trip was boring or annoying. Ask: is the situation really frightening, or just unpleasant? The clues in the sentence tell you which.
explain: In history, the word has a special meaning. Trial by ordeal was an old way of judging whether someone was guilty, using a cruel test. The word trial is a clue that this history meaning is in use.
fact: An ordeal is a very hard, painful or frightening experience that lasts for some time.
fact: In history, trial by ordeal was a cruel test used in the Middle Ages to try to decide if someone was guilty.
fact: Trial by ordeal asked God to show the truth, for example by checking if a burn healed.
fact: Witnesses and juries of ordinary people were a fairer way of judging, and they slowly took over.
fact: In 1215 the Church told priests to stop taking part in trials by ordeal, and the custom faded away.
exercise: «The car journey was an ordeal.» Mia says this means the car was broken. What does it really mean? | The car was broken | The journey was dangerous and frightening | The car was brand new | *The journey was boring or annoying
exercise: What was trial by ordeal? | A kind of medicine for burns | A holiday with a long car journey | *A cruel test used to try to decide if someone was guilty | A fair court where ordinary people sat as jurors
exercise: In «a terrible ordeal», what does the word terrible tell you? | It tells you the experience was bad | It tells you the experience was fun | It tells you nothing at all about the ordeal | *It tells you the experience was bad and hard to get through
test: «He survived a terrible ordeal in the mountains.» What does ordeal mean? | *A very hard, painful or frightening experience that lasts for some time | A type of mountain bird | A very hard, painful or frightening experience | A small holiday
test: Trial by ordeal was used to decide what? | When to plant crops | *Whether someone was guilty | Which day was a holiday | Who would win the castle
exam: In «the Church told priests to stop taking part, and it faded away», what does faded away suggest? | It was held every year | It got brighter | *It slowly stopped being used | It was moved to a new castle
